==Features==
Using a '''Satisfiability Solver''' to compute package dependencies. Its based on expressing [[Package_management#Package_dependencies|package dependencies]] as a [[wikipedia:Boolean_satisfiability_problem|boolean satisfiability problem]].

* See [http://files.opensuse.org/opensuse/en/b/b9/Fosdem2008-solver.pdf FOSDEM 2008 presentation]
* See [http://tinyurl.com/yfpujd3 Michael Schroeder's FOSDEM 2008 video talk]

===Background & Information===

The sat solver implementation as it appears in openSUSE 11.0 is based on two major, but independent, blocks

# Using a dictionary approach to store and retrieve package and dependency information.
# Using satisfiability, a well known and researched topic, for computing package dependencies.

The basics of using a satisfiability solver to solve package dependencies are detailed in [[openSUSE:Libzypp satsolver basics|SAT solver basics]] and [[openSUSE:Libzypp satsolver internals|SAT solver internals]] for more.

*See the [http://git.opensuse.org/autodocs/satsolver/HEAD/historypage.html history of SAT solver].
*See <!-- the [http://idea.opensuse.org/content/ideas/fast-installation-tool motivation], and -->the available [http://files.opensuse.org/opensuse/en/b/b9/Fosdem2008-solver.pdf FOSDEM2008 presentation].

